From: OpenDesk Agent
Subject: [PATCH] Modify libgcab to compile as static library for gio type system compatibility

This patch modifies libgcab/meson.build to compile libgcab as a static library
instead of a shared library. This is necessary on OpenHarmony platform where
glib, gio, and gobject are compiled as static libraries (.a) rather than shared
libraries (.so).

Problem:
- When libgcab is compiled as a shared library, it embeds gio static library
- This causes GObject type system to be defined twice (in libgcab.so and gcab)
- Result: G_IS_FILE check fails, GFile object creation fails
- gcab cannot create cabinet files

Solution:
- Compile libgcab as static library to avoid type system conflicts
- gcab executable statically links all gio/glib libraries
- No duplicate type system definitions

Tested:
- gcab --version: PASS
- gcab create: PASS (creates cabinet files successfully)
- gcab list: PASS (lists cabinet contents)
- gcab extract: PASS (extracts files correctly)
- File integrity: PASS (extracted files match originals)

---
 libgcab/meson.build | 14 +++++---------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libgcab/meson.build b/libgcab/meson.build
index original..modified 100644
--- a/libgcab/meson.build
+++ b/libgcab/meson.build
@@ -30,13 +30,9 @@
   subdir : 'libgcab-1.0/libgcab',
 )

-mapfile = 'libgcab.syms'
-vflag = '-Wl,--version-script,@0@/@1@'.format(meson.current_source_dir(), mapfile)
-libgcab = shared_library(
+# Compile as static library to avoid gio type system conflicts on OpenHarmony
+# (glib/gio/gobject are static libraries on this platform)
+libgcab = static_library(
   'gcab-1.0',
-  version : lt_version,
-  darwin_versions: darwin_versions,
-  link_args : cc.get_supported_link_arguments([vflag]),
-  link_depends : mapfile,
   enums,
   sources : [
     'gcab-cabinet.c',
@@ -49,6 +45,7 @@
   dependencies : [
     gio,
     libz,
   ],
   c_args : cargs,
   include_directories : [
     include_directories('.'),
     include_directories('..'),
   ],
+  install : true
 )

